            <ArticleTitle>Spinal cord stimulation combined with microsurgical DREZotomy for pain due to syringomyelia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>585-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/02688697.2016.1173187</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 49-year-old man with lower extremity neuropathic pain thought to be caused by spinal cord syringomyelia was treated with a combination of using spinal cord stimulation, decompression of the syrinx, relief of arachnoid adhesions and microsurgical DREZotomy. The patient had significant pain relief and has stable neurological status at follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
